{"slug":"14-01-ratios-rates-proportions-and-units-1-2-3","title":"14.01 Ratios, Rates, Proportions, and Units 1, 2 & 3","subject":"ESSENTIALS","total":51,"questions":[{"id":26371,"html":"<p>For a person m miles from a flash of lightning, the length of the time interval from the moment the person sees the lightning to the moment the person hears the thunder is k seconds. The ratio of m to k can be estimated to be 1 to 5. According to this estimate, the person is how many miles from a flash of lightning if the time interval is 25 seconds?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":97671,"html":"<p>10</p>","correct":false},{"id":97672,"html":"<p>9</p>","correct":false},{"id":97673,"html":"<p>6</p>","correct":false},{"id":97674,"html":"<p>5</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26372,"html":"<p>A group of monarch butterflies migrated from Chicago, Illinois, to Michoacn, Mexico, flying a total of 2,100 miles. It took a single butterfly in the group 120 days to travel this route one way. On average, how many miles did the butterfly travel per day?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":97675,"html":"<p>0.057</p>","correct":false},{"id":97676,"html":"<p>0.729</p>","correct":false},{"id":97677,"html":"<p>17.5</p>","correct":true},{"id":97678,"html":"<p>24</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26373,"html":"<p>In a box of pens, the ratio of black pens to red pens is 8 to 1. There are 40 black pens in the box. How many red pens are in the box?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":97679,"html":"<p>5</p>","correct":true},{"id":97680,"html":"<p>8</p>","correct":false},{"id":97681,"html":"<p>40</p>","correct":false},{"id":97682,"html":"<p>320</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26374,"html":"<p>The population density of Worthington is 290 people per square mile. Worthington has a population of 92,800 people. What is the area, in square miles, of Worthington?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":97683,"html":"<p>102,400</p>","correct":false},{"id":97684,"html":"<p>93,090</p>","correct":false},{"id":97685,"html":"<p>320</p>","correct":true},{"id":97686,"html":"<p>32</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26375,"html":"<p>A wind turbine completes 900 revolutions in 50 minutes. At this rate, how many revolutions per minute does this turbine complete?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":97687,"html":"<p>18</p>","correct":true},{"id":97688,"html":"<p>850</p>","correct":false},{"id":97689,"html":"<p>950</p>","correct":false},{"id":97690,"html":"<p>1,400</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26376,"html":"<p></p><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://nobin.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/summernote/Jm00uEXBmR1Dvy2Jb8SxjMWT6ngVPUdEHvBuJp82.png\" style=\"width: 178.991px;\"></div><br>In the table above, the ratio of y to x for each ordered pair is constant. What is the value of k?<p></p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":97691,"html":"<p>28</p>","correct":false},{"id":97692,"html":"<p>36</p>","correct":false},{"id":97693,"html":"<p>80</p>","correct":false},{"id":97694,"html":"<p>100</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26377,"html":"<p>The ratio of t to u is 1 to 2, and t = 10. What is the value of u?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":97695,"html":"<p>2</p>","correct":false},{"id":97696,"html":"<p>5</p>","correct":false},{"id":97697,"html":"<p>10</p>","correct":false},{"id":97698,"html":"<p>20</p>","correct":true}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26378,"html":"<p>How many yards are equivalent to 612 inches? (1 yard = 36 inches)</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":97699,"html":"<p>0.059</p>","correct":false},{"id":97700,"html":"<p>17</p>","correct":true},{"id":97701,"html":"<p>576</p>","correct":false},{"id":97702,"html":"<p>22,032</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26379,"html":"<p>Shaquan has 7 red cards and 28 blue cards. What is the ratio of red cards to blue cards that Shaquan has?</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":97703,"html":"<p>1 to 4</p>","correct":true},{"id":97704,"html":"<p>4 to 1</p>","correct":false},{"id":97705,"html":"<p>1 to 7</p>","correct":false},{"id":97706,"html":"<p>7 to 1</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26380,"html":"<p>A kangaroo has a mass of 28 kilograms. What is the kangaroo's mass, in grams? (1 kilogram = 1,000 grams)</p>","description":"","explanation":"","type":"mcq","multiColumn":false,"options":[{"id":97707,"html":"<p>28,000</p>","correct":true},{"id":97708,"html":"<p>1,028</p>","correct":false},{"id":97709,"html":"<p>972</p>","correct":false},{"id":97710,"html":"<p>784</p>","correct":false}],"selected":"","wasCorrect":false},{"id":26381,"html":"<p>The weight of an object on Venus is approximately&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{9}{10}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span style=\"display:none\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.1901em;vertical-align:-0.345em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing re